@startuml
!theme plain

title Input & Preprocessing System - Component API
allow_mixing

' ============================================
' PUBLIC API
' ============================================
interface "InputPreprocessingAPI" as api {
  + load_video(filepath: Path, max_dimension: Option<u32>) -> Result<VideoFile>
  + load_audio(filepath: Path) -> Result<AudioFile>
}

note right of api
  **Public Interface**
  This component exposes two operations:
  1. Load video file → VideoFile (with optional resize)
  2. Load audio file → AudioFile (kept at original rate)
  
  **Memory Considerations:**
  • Video stored as compressed frames (decode on-demand)
  • Audio kept at original rate (~44kHz, ~10MB/min)
  • NO up-front resampling (saves massive memory)
  
  These are just decoded file data, not signals yet!
  No knowledge of timeline, effects, or UI.
end note

' ============================================
' OUTPUT DATA STRUCTURES
' ============================================
package "Output Data Structures" #LightYellow {
    class VideoFile {
        + metadata: VideoMetadata
        + compressed_frames: Vec<CompressedFrame>
        + decode_frame(index: usize) -> Option<RawFrame>
        + frame_count() -> usize
        + carrier_sample_rate() -> f64
    }
    
    class VideoMetadata {
        + width: u32
        + height: u32
        + fps: f64
        + duration_seconds: f64
        + pixel_format: PixelFormat
        + samples_per_frame: usize
        + carrier_sample_rate: f64
    }
    
    class CompressedFrame {
        + frame_index: usize
        + compressed_data: Vec<u8>
        + decode() -> RawFrame
    }
    
    class RawFrame {
        + frame_index: usize
        + width: u32
        + height: u32
        + pixels: Vec<u8>
        + pixel_format: PixelFormat
    }
    
    class AudioFile {
        + metadata: AudioMetadata
        + samples: Vec<f32>
        + sample_rate: f64
        + get_sample_range(start: usize, len: usize) -> &[f32]
    }
    
    class AudioMetadata {
        + sample_rate: f64
        + channels: u32
        + duration_seconds: f64
        + total_samples: usize
    }
}

VideoFile --> VideoMetadata
VideoFile --> CompressedFrame
CompressedFrame --> RawFrame : "decodes to"
AudioFile --> AudioMetadata

api ..> VideoFile : returns
api ..> AudioFile : returns

note bottom of VideoMetadata
  **Carrier Sample Rate Calculation:**
  carrier_sample_rate = fps × (width × height)
  samples_per_frame = width × height
  
  **Memory Reality Check:**
  • 240×180 @ 30fps = 1.3M samples/s (manageable)
  • HD 1080p @ 30fps = 186M samples/s (44GB/min uncompressed!)
  • Solution: Keep frames compressed, decode on-demand
  • Optional: Resize on import for lower memory usage
  
  Example (working resolution):
  30fps @ 240×180 = 1,296,000 samples/s/channel
end note

' ============================================
' INTERNAL IMPLEMENTATION
' ============================================
package "Internal Implementation" #LightBlue {
    component "FFmpeg Wrapper" as ffmpeg
    component "Video Frame Decoder" as video_decoder
    component "Audio Decoder" as audio_decoder
    component "Video Scaler (Optional)" as scaler
    component "Frame Compressor" as compressor
    component "Carrier Rate Calculator" as rate_calc
}

ffmpeg --> video_decoder
ffmpeg --> audio_decoder
video_decoder --> scaler : "if max_dimension set"
scaler --> compressor
video_decoder --> compressor : "if no resize"

note bottom of ffmpeg
  Internal decoder implementation.
  Uses FFmpeg/libav for format support.
  Handles all video/audio codecs.
end note

note bottom of scaler
  **Optional Video Resizing:**
  • Reduce resolution on import if needed
  • Example: 1080p → 240p saves ~95% memory
  • Maintains aspect ratio
  • Uses high-quality scaling (Lanczos)
end note

note right of compressor
  **Frame Storage Strategy:**
  • Keep frames compressed (PNG, JPEG, or codec-specific)
  • Decode only when needed by effect graph
  • Typical compression: 10:1 to 20:1
  • Trade: CPU for memory
end note

note bottom of audio_decoder
  **Audio Storage:**
  • Kept at ORIGINAL sample rate (44.1kHz)
  • Linear interpolation done in real-time
  • ~10MB per minute vs ~10GB resampled
  • 1000x memory savings!
end note

@enduml

